      "summary": {
        "unit_id": "hmh-bridge:HMH-BRIDGE-ENTITY-CLEANUP:disconnect-ownership",
        "answer": "The compared event_handler[player_disconnect] body1200-1208 requests these operations in statement order: self notify(#death)1202; self.player_disconnected=1 at1203; self notify(#disconnect)1204; level notify(#disconnect,self)1205; unguarded [[level.callbackplayerdisconnect]]()1206; callback(#on_player_disconnect)1207. Actual native posting, self identity, payload, key normalization, delivery and continuation after any failure are unproved. Source convention uses the disconnecting player as receiver; it does not prove runtime class disjointness from every possible scene binding. The separately traced scene producer4484 uses a cscene instance created at scene_shared1587. Server remove_callback_on_death184-190 requests a watch-key notify, installs watch-key endon, then util::waittill_either(\"death\",\"remove_callbacks\"). That helper626-630 installs endon(msg1) and waittill(msg2). Only if con [excerpt; exact source record identified separately]",
        "behavior": "Compare ordered disconnect notifications and callback requests with conditional server watcher cleanup, guarded tombstoning and the different CSC wait-then-removal source path. Watcher189 runs only after normal wait continuation; _delay single_thread follows its armed endons/wait. Actual cancellation, persistent retention/deliverability and runtime player-versus-scene ownership remain unknown. Scene disconnect consumer 3621-3627 requires isdefined(level.gameended) AND !level.gameended before its set_igc_active(0) request. Registration/source ordering is not observed dispatch, cleanup or native success.",
        "unknowns": [
          "g3 A.1: native posting site/order/self-contract of player_disconnect and eventstruct fields (REA locator set itemized by g3; unchanged)",
          "N1: retail per-VM bundle set gating wz disconnect-handler execution and any scene route in an original CUSA11100 HMH session",
          "N4: notify delivery/cancellation ordering within the disconnect handler (1202/1204 vs 1205 vs 1206) and watcher-cancellation timing",
          "Whether any entry remains after actual disconnect, other removals and entity destruction, and whether any later delivery is valid; no permanent retention/deliverability guarantee.",
          "Original client death delivery and dynamic/external cleanup routes; the bounded saved CSC literal lookup found no remove_callbacks producer."
        ],
